    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG are delighted to present 41 Grosvenor Park to the market, a beautifully presented four-bedroom home enjoying a particularly attractive position within this highly regarded development just off Leinster Road in the heart of Rathmines. Arranged over three well-proportioned levels and presented in excellent condition throughout, the property offers bright, stylish and highly versatile accommodation ideally suited to modern family living. A standout feature of No. 41 is its wonderful position directly overlooking the communal green to the front, providing an attractive leafy outlook and a lovely sense of openness from the house. This peaceful setting, combined with the convenience of such a central Dublin 6 location, makes Grosvenor Park an especially appealing place to call home.\n\nThe accommodation is generous and thoughtfully arranged, with a welcoming entrance hallway leading to the kitchen and a comfortable living room. Across the upper floors are four excellent double bedrooms and two bathrooms. One of the top-floor bedrooms also benefits from an additional adjoining space, currently styled as a home office but equally well suited for use as a walk-in wardrobe, providing excellent flexibility depending on the needs of the new owners. The house has been very well maintained and is presented in turnkey condition throughout, allowing its new owners to move in with little more to do. Outside, the rear garden extends to approximately 35 feet, providing an attractive and private outdoor space, while to the front there is a designated parking space along with additional on-street parking within the development.\n\nThe location is exceptionally convenient, combining a quiet residential setting with everything Rathmines has to offer just moments away. Rathmines Village is within an easy five-minute walk, with its excellent choice of cafés, restaurants, shops and everyday amenities, while Rathgar, Ranelagh, Portobello and Harold's Cross are all within easy reach. There is also an abundance of attractive outdoor spaces nearby, including the Grand Canal, Harold's Cross Park, Belgrave Square and Palmerston Park. With its four double bedrooms, excellent presentation, flexible accommodation and particularly attractive outlook over the communal green, No. 41 offers an excellent opportunity to acquire a stylish and spacious home in one of Dublin 6's most sought-after residential settings."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nLiving Room - \n4.68 m × 4.65 m\n\nKitchen - \n3.09 m × 2.93 m\n\nEntrance Hall - \n3.12 m × 1.58 m\n\nBedroom 1 - \n3.67 m × 2.87 m\n\nBedroom 2 - \n3.28 m × 2.87 m\n\nBathroom - \n2.56 m × 1.63 m\n\nLanding - \n5.19 m × 1.67 m\n\nBedroom 3 - \n3.42 m × 2.89 m\n\nBedroom 4 - \n3.84 m × 2.89 m\n\nBathroom - \n2.70 m × 1.66 m\n\nLanding - \n3.48 m × 1.66 m\n\nStudy - \n1.86 m × 1.70 m\n\n"
      },
      {
